  <name>Libre VMM</name>
  <summary>A libre alternative to VMware Workstation</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Libre VMM is a QEMU/KVM-based virtual machine manager with a modern
      egui-based GUI, a REST API, a CLI, and support for 24 guest architectures.
      Built in Rust for security and reliability.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Live migration between hosts (VMware Workstation can't)</li>
      <li>GPU passthrough — single GPU + multi-GPU + Looking Glass</li>
      <li>LUKS-encrypted disks, TPM 2.0 emulation</li>
      <li>Per-VM nftables firewall rules</li>
      <li>Cloud-init / autounattend.xml unattended installs</li>
      <li>Native Wayland support</li>
      <li>Import from VMware (.vmx), VirtualBox (.vbox), Libvirt XML, Quickemu (.conf)</li>
      <li>Declarative VM configs in TOML or YAML — diffable, version-controllable</li>
      <li>REST API with OpenAPI spec — Terraform/Ansible-friendly</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">org.libre_vmm.LibreVmm.desktop</launchable>
